{
	"_doc": "Peoples of the strategic sim, built only from SRD 5.2.1 content. species/lineage name SRD species (drow is the Elf lineage). people: stat block for non-combatants. Recipes are [slug, weight] lists of SRD monster stat blocks; a party of n is allocated by largest remainder. mobility: route classes caravans and migrants use (road = surface road, deep = deep road, link = a route joining a deep site to the surface). raid_mobility: classes raiders and armies use. bands/biomes: where the culture settles, with weights; a biome left out weighs 0.4 and every generated biome is named for the surface peoples, so a misfit is a choice. farm/craft/luxury scale production. soldiers: garrison as a fraction of population. raid: base raiding drive. Optional (docs/tracks/peoples-below.md): tags ('deep': a people of the Underdark, drawn as species:deep, e.g. deep dwarves are dwarves with the deep tag, since SRD 5.2.1 has no lineage for them or for deep gnomes); makes: good -> how much more (over 1) or less (under 1) of it their land gives them (it scales the land's share, so the price and stockpile follow: a people that doesn't make a good buys it); wants: good -> how much more of it they keep in store (it scales the stock target, so they pay more for it); roles: the SRD stat block each role of their people is built from with make_npc (townsfolk, keeper, merchant, smith, priest, mage, guard, scout, raider); first_roles: who a settlement shows first, by tier, in place of data/life/people.json; estranged: relations lost with every other people; trade_floor: relations under which their caravans won't go to a people (default -20); stance: how they meet players, see data/life/standing.json and docs/tracks/peoples-below.md (abroad: hostile away from home until standing reaches spare_at; toll: what a player pays at the gate of their town (coin by tier, or a favour of standing; free at free_at; good for days; their people turn on one who is margin tiles inside the outermost building unpaid for grace_s); friendly_at: their own line for friendly); goes_down: their caravans take a way at their own town down to the deep town at its foot (only there: mobility still rules every other trip); raids_up: how much more a surface road reached by a way up weighs to their raiders in the deeps (docs/tracks/raids-below.md; 1 when absent). ",
